### Explanation:
This program continuously reads the analog output of a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 10‑bit ADC on SPI0 CE0, using channel 0 (CH0) of the ADC, samples the sensor once every 60 seconds in an infinite loop, and appends each measurement to a file named moisture_log.txt as a comma‑separated line containing an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp and the raw 10‑bit ADC value (0‑1023).

The program opens the SPI device file in read/write mode and sets the SPI mode and speed using the ioctl() system call. It then sets up a signal handler to catch SIGINT and SIGTERM signals and sets a flag to stop the infinite loop when one of these signals is received.

The program then opens the file for appending and enters an infinite loop. In each iteration, the program constructs an SPI transfer message containing the channel number and the start bit, and then transfers the message to the ADC using the write() system call. It then reads the received message using the read() system call and extracts the ADC value from the received message.

The program checks if the ADC value is within the valid range (0‑1023) and prints an error message and exits if it is not. If the value is valid, it gets the current time using the clock_gettime() function and formats it as an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp. It then writes the timestamp and the ADC value to the file using the fprintf() function.

The program waits for the next reading by calling the sleep() function for 60 seconds.

Finally, the program closes the SPI device file and the file before exiting.

### Note:
This program assumes that the SPI device file is located at /dev/spidev0.0 and that the MCP3008 ADC is connected to SPI0 CE0. It also assumes that the soil moisture sensor is connected to channel 0 of the ADC.

