# Embedded C Programming

## Introduction

This repository contains my solutions to the Embedded C Programming course on Coursera.

## Course Description

Embedded C programming is a hands-on course that teaches the fundamentals of embedded C programming. The course covers the basics of embedded C programming, including memory management, pointers, and data structures. It also covers advanced topics such as interrupt handling, real-time programming, and inter-process communication. The course includes a project that teaches students how to write a complete, compilable C program that fulfils the user's request exactly.

## Course Objectives

By the end of this course, students will be able to:

- Write complete, compilable C code that fulfils the user's request exactly.
- Use modern libraries (libgpiod or pigpio, never wiringPi); check every init and syscall, handle errors, and release resources on all exit paths.
- Output only the code.

## Course Syllabus

- Introduction to Embedded C Programming
- Memory Management
- Pointers
- Data Structures
- Interrupt Handling
- Real-Time Programming
- Inter-Process Communication
- Project

