The program starts by initializing the SPI device and configuring it for 1 MHz, SPI mode 0, 8 bits per word, and channel 0. It then initializes the GPIO pin for output and sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

The main loop continuously reads the moisture level from the ADC and compares it to the threshold. If the moisture level drops below the threshold, the program activates the pump for 10 seconds, logs the event, and then sleeps for 60 seconds before reading the moisture level again.

The program uses the pigpio library to initialize and control the GPIO pin. It also uses the time library to get the current time and format it for logging.

The program handles errors by printing messages to stderr and exiting with an error code. It also ensures that the pump is turned off before exiting.

