The program opens the I2C device file, sets the slave address, and then enters a loop that continuously measures distance and logs it to a CSV file.

The i2c_read() function performs a combined write-then-read transaction to read a register from the I2C device. It writes the register address to the device, then reads the specified number of bytes from the device.

The i2c_write() function writes a value to a register on the I2C device. It writes the register address and the value to the device.

The i2c_init() function opens the I2C device file and sets the slave address using ioctl(). It returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure.

The csv_init() function opens the CSV file and writes the header line. It returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure.

The measure_distance() function performs a distance measurement by writing the measurement start command to the I2C device, reading the measurement status register, and then reading the distance measurement register. It returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure.

