The program starts by opening the GPIO chip and getting the LED and touch lines. It then requests the LED line as an output and sets it to LOW. It then requests the touch line for rising edge events.

The program then sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to clean up resources and exit gracefully.

The program then enters a loop that waits for touch line events. When an event is received, it calls the debounce function to wait for 50 milliseconds and then toggles the LED.

If any of the driver calls fail, the program prints an error message and exits with an error code.

The program then cleans up resources and exits.

This program demonstrates how to use the libgpiod library to read touch input from a SainSmart TTP223B capacitive touch sensor connected on the GPIO bus, using the sensor’s OUT line on GPIO17 (physical pin 11) to capture rising‑edge events and toggles an LED attached to GPIO18 (physical pin 12) on each detected touch.

