### Explanation:
This program uses the libgpiod library to monitor the digital OUT of a KY‑038 sound sensor on GPIO17 (BCM) using a 100 ms polling interval, and when a sound event is detected it activates a 5 V relay connected to GPIO27 (BCM) for exactly 3 seconds, logging the timestamp of each activation to a file named alarm_log.txt.

The program opens the GPIO chip using gpiod_chip_open_by_name() and requests the sound sensor line using gpiod_line_request() with the request type set to GPIOD_LINE_REQUEST_EVENT_RISING_EDGE. It then sets up the relay line using gpiod_line_request_output() and opens the log file using fopen().

The program sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM using signal() to ensure a graceful shutdown when the program is interrupted.

The main loop of the program waits for a sound event using gpiod_line_event_wait() and checks if the sound sensor is still active using gpiod_line_get_value(). If the sound sensor is not active, the program continues to the next iteration of the loop.

If the sound sensor is active, the program checks if the relay is already active using relay_active. If the relay is already active, the program ignores the sound event and continues to the next iteration of the loop.

If the sound sensor is active and the relay is not active, the program activates the relay using gpiod_line_set_value() and sets relay_active to 1. It then gets the current time using clock_gettime() and logs the activation time to the log file using fprintf() and fflush().

The program then waits for the activation time to elapse using usleep(). After the activation time has elapsed, the program deactivates the relay using gpiod_line_set_value() and sets relay_active to 0.

If an error occurs during any of these operations, the program prints an error message and breaks out of the loop.

The program then cleans up by releasing the line using gpiod_line_release(), closing the GPIO chip using gpiod_chip_close(), and closing the log file using fclose().

The program returns 0 to indicate successful execution.

