### Explanation:
This program uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It initializes the library, opens the gpiochip0 device, requests the touch and relay lines, and sets up the touch interrupt service routine (ISR) to toggle the relay state on each rising edge.

The program also sets up a signal handler for SIGINT to ensure a clean shutdown when the user presses Ctrl+C. The handler forces the relay OFF, appends a final OFF entry to the log, releases the touch and relay lines, and closes the chip before exiting.

The program uses the gpiod_line_event_wait() and gpiod_line_event_read() functions to wait for and read touch events, and the gpiod_line_get_value() and gpiod_line_set_value() functions to read and write the relay state.

The program uses the gpiod_line_request_config struct to configure the touch and relay lines with the appropriate request type, consumer name, and flags. The touch line is requested with GPIOD_LINE_REQ_EV_BOTH_EDGES to trigger an interrupt on both rising and falling edges, and the relay line is requested with GPIOD_LINE_REQ_DIR_OUT to set the direction to output and GPIOD_LINE_REQUEST_FLAG_ACTIVE_LOW to invert the logic level.

The program uses the gpiod_line_request() function to request the touch and relay lines, and checks the return value to ensure that the request was successful. If any request fails, the program prints an error message and exits with EXIT_FAILURE.

The program uses the gpiod_line_set_value() function to set the initial relay state to OFF, and the log_state() function to log the initial state to the log file.

The program uses the signal() function to register the sigint_handler() function as the signal handler for SIGINT. The handler forces the relay OFF, appends a final OFF entry to the log, releases the touch and relay lines, and closes the chip before exiting.

The program uses the gpiod_line_event_wait() and gpiod_line_event_read() functions to wait for and read touch events. If the event type is GPIOD_LINE_EVENT_RISING_EDGE, the program calls the toggle_relay() function to toggle the relay state.

The program returns 0 to indicate successful execution.

