This program demonstrates how to use the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi, how to set up an interrupt service routine (ISR) to toggle the relay state on each rising edge of the touch sensor, and how to handle errors and cleanly exit the program when the user presses Ctrl+C.

