# Haptic Feedback Pattern Generator

This repository contains a C program that generates randomized haptic feedback patterns on two Precision Microdrives 310-101 eccentric rotating mass (ERM) vibration motors connected via GPIO (PWM), with Motor 1 driven on GPIO 17 (BCM) and Motor 2 on GPIO 27 (BCM); each pattern must consist of a sequence of 5 to 15 steps, each step specifying a PWM duty cycle from 0 to 255 for each motor and a step duration between 50 ms and 200 ms, using the appropriate API calls for PWM control and timing, seeding the random number generator with time(NULL), checking the API call return values, verifying that the GPIO mode is set correctly, handling any memory allocation failures, and running indefinitely to generate and play new random patterns until a SIGINT (Ctrl+C) is received, at which point a volatile sig_atomic_t shutdown flag should trigger a graceful shutdown that stops both motors and releases all resources.

## Usage

To compile and run the program, follow these steps:

1. Clone the repository: `git clone https://github.com/your-username/haptic-feedback-pattern-generator.git`
2. Navigate to the repository directory: `cd haptic-feedback-pattern-generator`
3. Compile the program: `gcc -o haptic-feedback-pattern-generator haptic-feedback-pattern-generator.c -lpigpio`
4. Run the program: `./haptic-feedback-pattern-generator`

